  "name": null,
  "problem": "A hospital administrator observed that the growth of the number of occupied beds in a hospital is directly proportional to the difference between the hospital’s maximum bed capacity and the current number of occupied beds. Let $H(t)$ be the number of occupied beds, measured in beds, and let $t\\ge 0$ be the time in years. If the maximum number of beds the hospital can support is $75$ beds, which differential equation could be used to model the number of occupied beds in the hospital? Assume that $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality.",
